# Pending queue UX

## Primary surface

Home = **pending / due / overdue / soon**. Not a calendar-first or stats-first shell.

## Task fields (MVP intent)

- Title
- Cadence (interval days and/or weekly/monthly rules)
- Estimated duration (minutes)
- Optional notes
- Next due / last completed
- Reminder time preference (global and/or per task)

## Actions

- **Done** — records completion, computes next due from rules
- **Snooze** — delays reminder/due without marking complete
- **Skip** this cycle (no reason field), pause, archive — in tree; skip-with-reason is not a goal

## Do

- Show duration on the pending row so planning is visible
- Keep the list short and scannable on a phone/tablet
- Prefer plain language (“Due today · ~15 min”) over jargon

## Do not

- Bury due items under habit heatmaps
- Require projects/tags to create a simple recurring chore
- Animate for its own sake on low-end devices
